; Entry point for `valk --build`.
; `--build` treats the script's last value as the entry and requires it to be
; a lambda. We can't reuse main.valk because its last form is `(lsp/start)`,
; which would execute the server at build time instead of at runtime.

(load "lsp/lsp.valk")
; lsp/start returns the LSP exit code (0 after `shutdown`, else 1), and
; --build uses the entry's numeric result as the process exit status.
(\ {argv} {lsp/start})
